---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/CourseLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
import { withBase } from "astro-theme-university/url";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`Eleven tutorials across weeks 2–12: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    No tutorial in week 1. Tutorials are hands-on, 90-minute labs in weeks 2–12:
    Thursdays, 2–3.30 pm, Systems Lab 2, starting 4 March.
    Bring the earlier artefact named on each
    page and leave with reproducible working. All data is synthetic; solo work
    is accepted throughout. Teaching pauses from 5–18 April.
  </p>
  <p>Download the synthetic datasets and reference scorer from the <a href={withBase('/toolkit/')}>course toolkit</a> before your tutorial. Each page below names the preparation, exercise and artefact to keep.</p>
  <p>The four blocks on each tutorial page fill its 90 minutes. The corresponding <a href={withBase('/lectures/')}>lecture plan</a> identifies the 60-minute lecture selection and about 210 minutes of independent preparation and consolidation. Bring existing working for review; the full teaching pack supplies examples across all three allocations.</p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
